A||||3||DJRice||annoying rattle from drivers side
Z||000000||DJRice||07-09-99||07:11 AM||||OK so I have this crazy rattle that I cant track down and Im wondering if it has plagued anyone elses cars.  It only happens when I am on a rough road.  It sounds like its coming from the drivers side of the car(87 SE V6), near the sail panel close to my head.  (I hope its not in my head) I have removed the louver panel, and the breather.  I have checked the gas cap and door.  What else is in that area that could produce this annoying  rattle?  
Z||000001||batboy||07-09-99||11:59 AM||||Due to normal wear on the hinge pins, door latch and striker, my door rattles sometimes on a rough road. In my case, I need to install new hinge pins and bushings. Sometimes the door glass rattles if the window seals are hard and cracked like most Fieros.
Z||000002||feffer||07-09-99||10:57 PM||||My recently purchased 87 has a noise coming from the driver's door. I drove it today for only the second time and determined that it was the door by simply holding onto it while I went over a some bumps to see if it still rattled. (I don't recommend it while you're on a turn, it is a little tough if you have a manual trans and a steering wheel that pulls a little like I do)<br>     In my case the hinge pins seem fine. I guess the striker/latch is the problem. It sounds and feels like the door just isn't latched even though it is. It just needs to latch tighter.
Z||000003||mwbackus||07-10-99||12:52 AM||||Temporary fix(s) for door noise :<p>Take a strip of velcro (the felt part) and wrap it around the striker.<p>Cut a piece of 1/2" polyetheylene tube and slit the side so it can wrap around the striker. <p>Either methods works, I use the tubing and I have never heard a peep out of my door since.
